h2("4.4 Algorithms Utilized in Existing Systems")
body('A comparative analysis of the algorithms and approaches used in existing AI assistant systems provides important context for understanding Dione\'s technical contributions. Traditional virtual assistants such as Siri, Alexa, and Google Assistant use Intent Classification Algorithms that map user input to a fixed set of predefined commands. These systems rely on supervised learning models trained on labeled datasets of user utterances and corresponding intents. While effective for a bounded set of supported commands, this approach cannot handle novel requests that fall outside the predefined intent taxonomy.')
body('Sequence-to-Sequence Models form the foundation of modern LLMs and are used for text generation tasks including translation, summarization, and dialogue generation. These models use encoder-decoder architectures with attention mechanisms to generate output sequences conditioned on input sequences. While powerful for text generation, these models lack the ability to interact with external systems or execute actions in the real world.')
body('Chain-of-Thought (CoT) Reasoning, introduced by Wei et al., enables language models to perform complex reasoning tasks by generating intermediate reasoning steps before producing a final answer. This technique significantly improves performance on mathematical, logical, and commonsense reasoning tasks. However, CoT reasoning is limited to generating text-based reasoning traces and does not include any mechanism for executing actions or interacting with external tools.')
body('The ReAct Algorithm, which Dione adopts as its core operational paradigm, combines the strengths of chain-of-thought reasoning with the ability to take actions and observe results. By interleaving reasoning and acting, ReAct enables language models to dynamically adjust their approach based on real-world feedback, making it uniquely suited for agentic AI applications. Search and Retrieval Algorithms based on RAG are used for context enhancement by retrieving relevant information from external knowledge bases to supplement the model\'s parametric knowledge.')
body('The fundamental limitation of existing systems is that they either focus on reasoning (generating text-based plans and instructions) or on execution (carrying out predefined workflows) but fail to integrate both capabilities securely within a local environment. Dione addresses this limitation by combining ReAct-based reasoning with a secure, plugin-based execution framework that operates entirely on the user\'s device.')

